From c408d364daab1014014a7b8dcd4403e07c580340 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:06:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] bfd: k1om: 4 KiB pages, not the Solaris 1 MiB of the
 vector above

The restored k1om vectors follow x86_64_elf64_sol2_vec, which sets
ELF_MAXPAGESIZE to 0x100000, and inherited it (upstream reset it in the
l1om block in between, which is not restored).  With a 1 MiB minimum page
size GDB rejected the PIE load displacement (breakpoints stayed at the
unrelocated addresses) and placed shared libraries at 1 MiB boundaries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
---
 bfd/elf64-x86-64.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bfd/elf64-x86-64.c b/bfd/elf64-x86-64.c
index dd8ba8dc197..398a2e7bbdc 100644
--- a/bfd/elf64-x86-64.c
+++ b/bfd/elf64-x86-64.c
@@ -6491,6 +6491,10 @@ elf64_k1om_elf_object_p (bfd *abfd)
 #undef elf_backend_object_p
 #define elf_backend_object_p		    elf64_k1om_elf_object_p
 
+/* Not the Solaris 1MB page size of the vector above.  */
+#undef	ELF_MAXPAGESIZE
+#define ELF_MAXPAGESIZE			    0x1000
+
 /* Restore defaults.  */
 #undef ELF_TARGET_OS
 
